    <h2 class="hs">How I work</h2>
    <div class="g3">
      <div class="c"><h3>Clarity before code</h3><p>Backend-heavy systems hide their risk in edge cases. I turn open questions into agreed scenarios with the client and the team first, so rework stays cheap.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Make status visible</h3><p>Every handoff should show where it stands, in the product and in Jira, not in messages that get missed.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Keep scope honest</h3><p>Infrastructure, extras and new ideas become visible change requests with estimates, so the client always knows what they are choosing.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Write it down</h3><p>Requirements, flow designs and user manuals are living documents with version history, so knowledge does not leave when people do.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Plan around dependencies</h3><p>Specifications, credentials and test environments often come from third parties. I track them as dated risks with owners.</p></div>
      <div class="c"><h3>Prototype to align</h3><p>I wireframe and build small prototypes so conversations with designers and developers stay concrete.</p></div>
    </div>

